---
description: Specs are law; notes are scrapbook; plans are execution
alwaysApply: true
---

# Document authority

| Location | Role | Git |
|---|---|---|
| `specs/` | Normative product + computation + API + UI | commit |
| `plans/` | Slice sequence and done-when | commit |
| `docs/` | Explanatory primers (maps, not law) | commit |
| `_notes/` | Research scrapbook (non-binding) | ignore |
| `_notes/founding/` | Locked historical brief | ignore; never edit |

If a spec and a note disagree, **the spec wins**. Do not implement solely from `_notes/`. Primers in `docs/` explain the running app and the test suite; they are not a second spec. If a primer and a spec disagree, **the spec wins** — then patch the primer.

## Graduate, then build

Trade date, expected grid, OHLCV, VWAP, schema, DQ rules/score, API payloads, and UI behaviour belong in `specs/`, not in rules and not as living law in `_notes/`.

If the spec is still a summary and the detail lives only under `_notes/cursor/`, **promote that slice into `specs/` before treating it as implementation law**. Leave the note as archaeology or mark it superseded.

## Spec evolution

Amend in place. No `*-v2.md`, no copies into `_notes/founding/` or `plans/archive/`. Git is the version trail. A one-line revision (date + sentence) at the top of a spec is enough; do not keep a long changelog in the file.

| Change | Edit | Then |
|---|---|---|
| Scope, personas, v1 vs extension, architecture | `specs/loupe-solution-design.md` | New `plans/` slice if work remains |
| UI chrome, KPIs, tooltips, wireframes | `specs/loupe-ui-design.md` | Keep solution §12 as pointer + invariants |
| Formula, grid, DDL, rule IDs, API shapes, sample claims | The sibling spec that owns it | Research may start in `_notes/`; promote before it is law |
| Locked decisions (solution brief §3) | Rewrite the numbered item; do not leave two truths | Grep `plans/` and other specs for the old sentence |
| Sequence / done-when only | `plans/` | Do not shadow-spec |
| How the running app or tests are wired | the matching `docs/` primer | Keep `specs/` as the pointer for truth |

Conflict after an edit: **intent / v1 boundary → spec**; **how a number is computed or what the sample contains → fix the spec** (notes are not a veto). Demo lessons that change product copy patch the UI spec the same day. Oracle lessons patch the analytics/sample spec, then one sentence in the brief if §3/§8 would still teach the wrong rule.

Post-v1 features: new numbered plan, and a spec subsection marked **extension** until promoted to v1. Do not reopen a `done` plan except to point at the spec change.

## Plans

- Committed. One index plus one file per slice (not solution vs UI).
- Done slices stay in place; mark done in the index. Move to `plans/archive/` only when **superseded**.
- Plans do not restate the design. Pointers only.

## Primers

- `docs/` explains the running app, page numbers, and the test suite. Maps, not law.
- Patch the matching primer in the same commit when the map would otherwise lie (`.cursor/rules/docs-on-commit.mdc`).

## Notes

- `_notes/` is a lab notebook: drafts, dead ends, raw measurements, working SQL.
- `_notes/founding/` is read-only. Do not keep founding in sync.
- Do not load the whole `_notes/` tree into a chat.
